        "id": "ex-five-assays-on-one-animal-versus-five-animals",
        "kind": "example",
        "title": "Five assays on one animal versus one assay on five animals",
        "statement": "With five total readings and biological variance 4 and technical variance 1, the average from one animal with five assays has variance 21/5, whereas five independently sampled animals with one assay each give variance 1 for the same population mean.",
        "strategy": "Apply the balanced-mean variance theorem to the two allocations of five readings, then compute their exact difference and the zero-biological-variance boundary.",
